    summary: `# 🦠 Zoonoses #13 — Emerging Zoonotic Diseases & Wildlife

## 🎯 EID concept
- **Emerging:** newly recognized OR increasing in incidence/geography
- **Re-emerging:** previously controlled, now resurging
- ~75% of EIDs are zoonotic
- ~70% from wildlife reservoirs
- Drivers: deforestation, wildlife trade, climate change, intensive farming

## 🔥 Recent EIDs

| Disease | Year | Origin | Reservoir |
|---|---|---|---|
| HIV | 1980s | Chimps | Primates |
| SARS | 2002 | Civets/bats | Bats |
| H5N1 AI | 1997 | Birds | Wild waterfowl |
| West Nile (USA) | 1999 | Mosquitoes | Birds |
| Nipah | 1998 | Pigs/bats | Fruit bats |
| MERS-CoV | 2012 | Camels | Bats |
| Ebola (W. Africa) | 2014 | Bushmeat | Bats |
| Zika (Americas) | 2015 | Mosquitoes | Primates |
| SARS-CoV-2 | 2019 | Bats? | Bats (likely) |
| Mpox (multi-country) | 2022 | Wildlife (Africa) | Rodents |

## 🦇 Bats as reservoirs
- ~1,400 species, 20% of mammals
- Long lifespan, communal roosting → virus persistence
- Unique immune adaptations (low inflammation, high IFN)
- **Major reservoirs:** SARS, MERS, SARS-CoV-2, Nipah, Hendra, Ebola, Marburg, rabies (Americas)
- Conservation: protect (ecosystem services) + surveillance (no culling)

## 🦌 Wildlife as reservoir/sentinel
- Deer (CWD, SARS-CoV-2)
- Rodents (hantavirus, plague, leptospirosis)
- NHPs (HIV ancestors, monkeypox, Marburg)
- Birds (AI, West Nile, salmonella)
- Marine mammals (anisakis, leptospirosis)

## 🌡️ Drivers of emergence

### Deforestation + land use change
- Habitat fragmentation → wildlife-livestock-human contact
- Bat-pig contact (Malaysia 1998 Nipah)
- Mining + Ebola spillover

### Wildlife trade
- Wet markets — high diversity, high contact
- Pangolins (intermediate for SARS-CoV-2?)
- Civets (SARS), monkeys (mpox)
- Bushmeat (Ebola, HIV)

### Intensive farming
- Pig amplifier (JE, Nipah, swine flu)
- Poultry amplifier (AI, Salmonella)
- Antibiotic use → AMR

### Climate change
- Vector range expansion (Aedes, Ixodes northward)
- Permafrost thaw — anthrax, ancient pathogens
- El Niño + leptospirosis

### Globalization + travel
- SARS spread via flights
- MERS South Korea outbreak (1 traveler)
- COVID-19 pandemic

## 🛡️ Pandemic preparedness
- **PREDICT** — USAID program (2009-2020), bat virus discovery
- **GVN** (Global Virome Network)
- **CEPI** (Coalition for Epidemic Preparedness Innovations)
- **Pandemic treaty** (WHO, in negotiation)
- **OneHealth** integration (WHO+WOAH+FAO+UNEP quadripartite 2022)

## 🇹🇭 Thailand wildlife surveillance
- **EID-AS Center** (CUVET) — Aj. Thiravat + Aj. Suchana et al.
- Bat species mapping (Pteropus, cave species)
- Wildlife trade interdiction (DNP, customs)
- Ranong Quarantine Station
- Khao Yai + national parks surveillance

## 📝 EXAM RECAP
1. ⭐ ~75% EIDs zoonotic, ~70% from wildlife
2. ⭐ Bats = key reservoir (SARS, MERS, COVID, Nipah, Ebola)
3. ⭐ Drivers: deforestation, wildlife trade, intensive farming, climate
4. ⭐ Pig = amplifier (JE, Nipah, swine flu)
5. ⭐ One Health quadripartite (WHO+WOAH+FAO+UNEP 2022)`,
